    "lawCode": "Amd §532, RWB L",
    "lawSection": "Racing, Pari-Mutuel Wagering and Breeding Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3452\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and\nbreeding law, in relation to the distribution of surcharges on\noff-track winnings\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :  To restore the provisions of\nChapter 681 of the Laws of 2007 which were mistakenly repealed by\nChapter 18 of 2008.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :  Adds back into law the requirement\nthat certain regional surcharge revenues are to continue to be\ndistributed to a harness track in Erie County.\n\n EFFECTS OF PRESENT LAW WHICH THIS BILL WOULD ALTER :  Restores the\nprovisions of an extension in law of the surcharge distribution from\n2007 to August 31, 2012 as provided for in Chapter 681 of 2007.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :  Chapter 681 of 2007 extended the provisions relating\nto the distribution of surcharge revenues from 2007 to 2012. However,\nbecause the effective date of that Chapter was 10.31.07, the drafters\nof subsequent 2008 legislation failed to notice the provisions of the\nOctober chapter and therefor considered the section which would have\notherwise expired as archaic and OK to repeal.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :  See Chapter 681 of 2007.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS :  None.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :  Immediately.\n",
